This property's direct injective-agreement proof in Tamarin exhausts memory
(>21 GB; OOM after ~56 min with --auto-sources and a tuned oracle) on an 8 GB
machine, because the fog node recovers SK by decrypting N_f, whose AEAD key
embeds two Diffie-Hellman values, making the backward search explode.
The property holds and is established by composition from the machine-verified
lemmas authA_CS_V and authA_CS_F together with the secrecy of k_jc (key_jc);
see Section VI of the paper. Re-running on a >=32-64 GB host may complete it.
